cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or refer to this framework, please cite it as below."
title: "Public Availability with Source-Code Visibility License (PASVL-1.0) and Letter of Software Deployment Approval (LOSDA-1.0)"
abstract: >-
  A source-available licensing framework in which software source code is permanently public and
  visible, while the right to deploy the software is granted individually through a Letter of
  Software Deployment Approval (LOSDA) — a named, scoped, time-limited, publicly registered
  permission instrument. The framework comprises a license (PASVL-1.0), an instrument
  specification (LOSDA-1.0), a public registry, governance policies, and templates.
